 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "Look at where the login check is registered in your admin bundle. It is almost certainly decorated with `@admin.before_any_request` and should be `@admin.before_request`.\n\n**Why**\n\n- `Bundle.before_any_request` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:614`) is documented as running \"before every request, not only those handled by the bundle.\" It registers via `record_once` into `app.before_request_funcs[None]`, which is the app-wide scope. Every request in the app runs it.\n- `Scaffold.before_request` (`src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:468`) on a bundle stores into the bundle's own `before_request_funcs`. When the bundle is registered, `bundles.py:402` merges those under the bundle's name. `preprocess_request` (`src/tessel/app.py:1385`) then runs them only for requests the bundle handles.\n\n**Fix**\n\nChange `@admin.before_any_request` to `@admin.before_request`. Keep `before_any_request` only for things that really are app-wide, like `load_logged_in_user` in `examples/tutorial/tesselr/auth.py:32`.\n\nAlso check that nothing in your admin bundle uses `before_any_request` for the check indirectly, for example through a shared helper or a bundle that is nested or registered twice.",
